  {
   "id": "hunt", "name": "Hunt", "stage": "gather", "where": "outside", "needs": "none", "priority": 75,
   "text": "Out hunting", "idle": "no game to hunt",
   "demand": "target", "offer": "hunt", "skill": "hunting",
   "inputs": {}, "outputs": {"carcass": 1},
   "note": "data/companion/hunt.json, scripts/companion/hunt_job.gd (the logic) and hunt_run.gd (the body): reads sign (the core's hunt.track), stalks and shoots real game, and hauls the kill home for the butcher or dresses it where it fell. The carcass is not a store kind: it links the hunt to the butcher in the chain (the meals, jerky, leather and furs shortages pull it through the butcher); the butcher is fed_from_outside too (the player's kills), so switching the hunt off never takes the butcher with it.",
   "keep": {}, "how": {"type": "survival", "action": "hunt.track", "result": "hunt"}, "tags": ["meat", "hide", "heavy"],
   "tools": {"need": [["musket", "over_under", "bow", "spear_pair", "pistol"]], "optional": [["trade_knife", "flint_knife"], ["climb_stakes"]],
    "use_by": {"musket": {"musket_balls": 4, "powder": 1}, "over_under": {"musket_balls": 4, "powder": 1}, "pistol": {"musket_balls": 4, "powder": 1}, "bow": {"arrows": 8}, "spear_pair": {}},
    "food": ["jerky", "johnnycake", "roast_venison", "roast_small_game", "roast_fish", "smoked_venison"],
    "note": "TOOLS/HUNT: a weapon (any of these; HuntKit takes the one she is best at that has shot for it: marksmanship, archery, close combat), a knife to dress the kill (optional), and per trip the shot for her weapon (use_by: the weapon's `use`, the whole units she takes: a pound of powder is 40 charges) and a meal from the store (food: the first there is). HuntKit checks them out of the pool (ToolPool.checkout / take), spends each shot fired and each arrow or spear lost (ToolPool.spend), and returns the rest after the hunt."}
  },
